2026-11-05T05:35:58+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: Key guidelines:
2026-11-05T05:35:58+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For list/set operations where order matters in the result, avoid using set() which randomizes order. Instead use sorted lists or preserve insertion order.
2026-11-05T05:35:58+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For "difference between two lists", return elements in one list but not the other (not symmetric difference), maintaining order.
2026-11-05T05:35:58+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For dictionary unique values, preserve sorted or insertion order rather than using set() directly.
2026-11-05T05:35:58+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For text/string analysis functions, consider that input may be a list/iterable rather than a string to split.
