2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For list/set operations where order matters, avoid set() which randomizes order; use sorted lists or preserve insertion order.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For "difference between two lists", return elements in one list but not the other (not symmetric difference), maintaining order.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For dictionary unique values, preserve sorted or insertion order.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For text/string analysis functions, consider that input may be a list/iterable rather than a string to split.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For rotation counting, find the index of the minimum element as the rotation count.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For IP validation, return True/False with careful edge case handling.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - When returning lists, match expected ordering (sorted if needed).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - When finding pairs (e.g., max product pair), return elements in their original array order.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For periodic/floor functions like floor_Min(A, B, N): test with simple cases carefully.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - Avoid defining the same function twice; write clean, single implementations.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - Keep solutions concise and correct.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For tuple matrix flattening into column tuples: zip(*test_list) gives columns; return list of tuples from zip.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For counting characters with vowel neighbors: count characters at positions where AT LEAST ONE neighbor is a vowel.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For splitting strings at uppercase letters: filter out empty strings; re.split(r'(?=[A-Z])', text) may produce leading empty string.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For quadratic equation reciprocal roots: roots are reciprocal when a == c; return "Yes"/"No" string.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For area/geometry functions, return integer results using // when formula yields whole number (e.g., rhombus area = (p*q)//2).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For sorting numeric strings, return a list of integers: sorted([int(x) for x in nums_str]).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For copying a list, if input is already a list just return list(xs).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For chain length problems with pairs: sort by second element, chain when arr[j][1] < arr[i][0] (strict less than).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For "convert string to list" problems, the expected result is likely splitting by spaces into words: return string.split(), not list(string) which gives individual characters.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For triangle type problems, check if sides form a valid triangle first; "Equilateral", "Isosceles", "Scalene" may need to be returned without "Triangle" suffix - check problem carefully.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For maximum sum with no three consecutive elements: dp[i] = max(dp[i-1], dp[i-2]+arr[i], dp[i-3]+arr[i-1]+arr[i]) but initialize carefully; dp[2] should be max(arr[0]+arr[1], arr[1]+arr[2], arr[0]+arr[2]).
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - Always test edge cases mentally before finalizing: empty inputs, single elements, boundary conditions.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - For area/geometry, use integer division when appropriate.
2026-11-05T06:51:54+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - When the problem says "copy a list", return list(xs) directly.
