2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - The query should help retrieve the specific Wikipedia article(s) that are the "bridge" documents in the multi-hop reasoning chain.
2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: Examples of good queries:
2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - A specific person's name (e.g., "Erik Watts wrestler" or "Bill Watts wrestler born 1939")
2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - A specific article title (e.g., "I Would Die 4 U Prince song Purple Rain")
2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: - A specific entity combination (e.g., "Boy Hits Car band discography studio albums")
2026-11-05T15:21:04+00:00 deckbox nice[4164997]: Avoid outputting just "True" or "False" as the query - always output a substantive search string targeting missing supporting documents.
